### Why this is better

Suppose the IDoc does this:

```text
LIKP updated
Z-table updated
COMMIT
```

Both succeed.

But if something fails:

```text
LIKP updated
Z-table updated
ERROR
ROLLBACK
```

then **both changes are rolled back**.

You don't end up with:

```text
LIKP = updated
Z-table = updated
```

when the IDoc ultimately goes into error.

