## The important distinction: IDoc status vs database commit

Be careful with the phrase **"IDoc is successful."**

There are actually two things:

1. The application processing has completed successfully.
2. The database LUW has committed.

You want the Z-table update to happen **before the commit but only after the application has successfully completed the relevant LIKP update**.

So ideally:

```text
IDoc processing
   ↓
LIKP successfully changed
   ↓
your enhancement
   ↓
Z-table update
   ↓
standard IDoc processing finishes
   ↓
SAP commits LUW
   ↓
IDoc becomes successful
```

Not:

```text
IDoc successful
   ↓
new program/job
   ↓
update Z-table
```

The second approach introduces a timing gap and race conditions.

